{"parents": [{"link": "../../../", "title": "Module code"}], "title": "auth0.authentication.revoke_token", "body": "<h1>Source code for auth0.authentication.revoke_token</h1><div class=\"highlight\"><pre>\n<span></span><span class=\"kn\">from</span> <span class=\"nn\">typing</span> <span class=\"kn\">import</span> <span class=\"n\">Any</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">from</span> <span class=\"nn\">.base</span> <span class=\"kn\">import</span> <span class=\"n\">AuthenticationBase</span>\n\n\n<div class=\"viewcode-block\" id=\"RevokeToken\">\n<a class=\"viewcode-back\" href=\"../../../../authentication/#auth0.authentication.revoke_token.RevokeToken\">[docs]</a>\n<span class=\"k\">class</span> <span class=\"nc\">RevokeToken</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">AuthenticationBase</span><span class=\"p\">):</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"sd\">&quot;&quot;&quot;Revoke Refresh Token endpoint</span>\n\n<span class=\"sd\">    Args:</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">        domain (str): Your auth0 domain (e.g: my-domain.us.auth0.com)</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">    &quot;&quot;&quot;</span>\n\n<div class=\"viewcode-block\" id=\"RevokeToken.revoke_refresh_token\">\n<a class=\"viewcode-back\" href=\"../../../../authentication/#auth0.authentication.revoke_token.RevokeToken.revoke_refresh_token\">[docs]</a>\n    <span class=\"k\">def</span> <span class=\"nf\">revoke_refresh_token</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"bp\">self</span><span class=\"p\">,</span> <span class=\"n\">token</span><span class=\"p\">:</span> <span class=\"nb\">str</span><span class=\"p\">)</span> <span class=\"o\">-&gt;</span> <span class=\"n\">Any</span><span class=\"p\">:</span>\n<span class=\"w\">        </span><span class=\"sd\">&quot;&quot;&quot;Revokes a Refresh Token if it has been compromised</span>\n\n<span class=\"sd\">        Each revocation request invalidates not only the specific token, but all other tokens</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">        based on the same authorization grant. This means that all Refresh Tokens that have</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">        been issued for the same user, application, and audience will be revoked.</span>\n\n<span class=\"sd\">        Args:</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">             token (str): The Refresh Token you want to revoke</span>\n\n<span class=\"sd\">         See: https://auth0.com/docs/api/authentication#refresh-token</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">        &quot;&quot;&quot;</span>\n        <span class=\"n\">body</span> <span class=\"o\">=</span> <span class=\"p\">{</span>\n            <span class=\"s2\">&quot;client_id&quot;</span><span class=\"p\">:</span> <span class=\"bp\">self</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">client_id</span><span class=\"p\">,</span>\n            <span class=\"s2\">&quot;token&quot;</span><span class=\"p\">:</span> <span class=\"n\">token</span><span class=\"p\">,</span>\n        <span class=\"p\">}</span>\n\n        <span class=\"k\">return</span> <span class=\"bp\">self</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">authenticated_post</span><span class=\"p\">(</span>\n            <span class=\"sa\">f</span><span class=\"s2\">&quot;</span><span class=\"si\">{</span><span class=\"bp\">self</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">protocol</span><span class=\"si\">}</span><span class=\"s2\">://</span><span class=\"si\">{</span><span class=\"bp\">self</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">domain</span><span class=\"si\">}</span><span class=\"s2\">/oauth/revoke&quot;</span><span class=\"p\">,</span> <span class=\"n\">data</span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"n\">body</span>\n        <span class=\"p\">)</span></div>\n</div>\n\n</pre></div>", "current_page_name": "_modules/auth0/authentication/revoke_token", "sidebars": ["localtoc.html", "relations.html", "sourcelink.html", "searchbox.html"], "alabaster_version": "1.0.0", "alabaster_version_info": [1, 0, 0], "sphinx_version_info": [8, 1, 3, "final", 0], "READTHEDOCS": false}